sition.\n3. snapshot s0.\n4. play_input no input 40 frames (or a bit less to avoid collision).\n5. snapshot s1.\n6. diff decreased (Goomba x decreasing) — name e1.\n\nBut wait: with no input, is Mario idle? Yes. Camera stays. So changed addresses: Goomba x, timer, RNG, animation counters (Mario idle animation? SMB Mario has a walking animation but idle is static; frame counters $0009). Enemy also has an animation timer.\n\nLet me do it.\n\nHowever, one concern: is the Goomba's x stored as a level x (large, decreasing) or as something else? In SMB, Enemy_X_Position is the level x position (0-255 within page), Enemy_PageLoc is the page. Goomba walks left, so x decreases and may wrap page. Fine.\n\nLet me scroll right 120 frames. Actually to get the Goomba on screen without Mario hitting it: the prompt says ~4 seconds (240 frames) of holding Right runs into the first Goomba. So at 120 frames, he's about halfway. Let's do 130 frames and check.\n\nActually the Goomba walks toward Mario, so collision at ~240 frames if Mario keeps walking. If I stop at 130, the Goomba continues left toward Mario at ~0.5px/frame while Mario is at ~130*1.5=195 px... Goomba spawns at enemy x maybe 0x1E page... hmm. Distance: Goomba at level x ~ 384? Mario at 195. Gap ~190 px, closing at 1.5+0.5=2px/frame → ~95 frames to collision. So I have ~90 frames of observation. A 40-frame window is fine.\n\nLet's go: play_input right 130 frames, then screenshot + list_sprites."}
