{"type":"thinking","text":"After writing $0087=100 and stepping 4: Goomba at screen x=240/248 (was 175/183). The screenshot shows the Goomba at the right edge (x~240). ✓ x proof complete.\n\nHmm, the screenshot sha is 943018... which was also the sha for an earlier screenshot. Hmm, that earlier screenshot was also after writing $0087 and showed the Goomba at 174? Let me look: the screenshot I'm seeing now — the Goomba is at the right (x~240), and the earlier 943018 screenshot I described also had the Goomba near the right edge. Hmm, earlier I said \"Goomba at ~180\" for 943018. Hmm. The image now shows the Goomba at the far right (x~240). OK, I'll trust list_sprites: 240. Good.\n\nNow everything is proven. Let me record the mappings and promote.\n\nMappings to record:\n\n1. type:\n```\nrecord_mapping(mapping_type=\"address\", id=\"0x0016\", name=\"enemy_type\", category=\"enemy\", group=\"enemy_object\", stride=1, count=6, format=\"binary enemy ID (Goomba = 6)\", source=\"differential search\", notes=\"...\")\n```\n\n2. x:\n```\nid=\"0x0087\", name=\"enemy_x_position\", stride=1, count=6, format=\"binary, low byte of level x (0-255); absolute level x = 0x006E*256 + 0x0087 for the first enemy\", ...\n```\n\n3. page:\n```\nid=\"0x006E\", name=\"enemy_x_page\", stride=1, count=6, format=\"binary page/high byte of the enemy's level x\", ...\n```\n\n4. y:\n```\nid=\"0x00CF\", name=\"enemy_y_position\", stride=1, count=6, format=\"binary screen y\"\n```\n\nLet me write good notes with the encoding and proof.\n\nNotes for type ($0016):\n\"Enemy object type/ID, one byte per slot: $0016-$001B = enemy slots 0-5 (stride 1, count 6). The enemy spawner at CPU $C12F-$C13C does LDA $06CD / STA $16,X (type) then LDA #$01 / STA $0F,X (Enemy_Flag) and STA $1E,X=$00 (state), so the same slot index X addresses this array, the x low byte at $87,X, the page at $6E,X and the y at $CF,X. In World 1-1 the first Goomba's slot held $06; while paused, write_memory $0016 = 11 and step_frame 3 turned the walking Goomba into a red Koopa Troopa: list_sprites returned sprite palette 5 with CHR tiles 165-169 (was palette 7, tiles 112-115) and the screenshot shows the red-shelled Koopa in the Goomba's place. Proves the byte selects the enemy type. (Note: writing 0 also kept a Goomba on screen.) Found with no reference by differential search + disassembly of the spawner.\"\n\nHmm, the \"note: writing 0 also kept a Goomba\" — maybe skip to keep it clean. I'll include a short parenthetical for honesty.\n\nNotes for x ($0087):\n\"Enemy object horizontal position, low byte of the level x, one byte per slot: $0087-$008C (stride 1, count 6; the same contiguous array starts one byte earlier at $0086 with the player at slot 0 and enemy 1 at $0086+1 = $0087). Absolute level x = $006E*256 + $0087; the routine at CPU $F171 (prgRom 0x717F) does LDA $86,X / SEC / SBC $071C / STA $03AD,Y, so the on-screen x is (low byte - scroll) mod 256. PROOF (write_memory + step + list_sprites, no reference): in World 1-1 the first Goomba's slot read $0087=34 with page $006E=1 (level x 290, screen x 174-175); write_memory $0087=100 (paused) and step_frame 4 put the drawn Goomba at OAM x=240/248 (screenshot: Goomba moved from mid-screen to the right edge, Mario unchanged); a second test wrote 80 and it appeared at 219. Also the enemy spawner stores the low byte with STA $87,X at CPU $C1B4.\"\n\nNotes for page ($006E):\n\"Enemy object level-x page (high byte), one byte per slot: $006E-$0073 (stride 1, count 6; the player's page is $006D). Absolute level x = $006E*256 + the $0087 slot. The spawner stores it with STA $6E,X at CPU $C1AB from $073A. PROOF (play_input watch, 110 frames, Goomba walking left with no input): $0087 stepped 33,32,...,1,0 then wrapped to 255,254,...,238 while $006E read 1 for samples up to frame 66 and flipped to 0 at frame 68 - exactly the frame the low byte wrapped 0->255 - so the pair is a 16-bit level position and this byte is its high half.\"\n\nNotes for y ($00CF):\n\"Enemy object vertical position, one byte per slot: $00CF-$00D4 (stride 1, count 6; the array starts at $00CE with the player's y and enemy 1 at $00CE+1 = $00CF). The routine at CPU $F171 does LDA $CE,X / STA $03B8,Y, so it is the screen y of the enemy (OAM y = value + 1). PROOF (write_memory + step + list_sprites): on the ground in 1-1 the Goomba's slot read $00CF=184 (OAM y 185); while paused, write_memory $00CF=140 and step_frame 13 lifted the drawn Goomba to OAM y=142/150/158 (screenshot/list_sprites show it floating above the ground) while the value kept its own gravity step 140->141. Also the spawner stores it with STA $CF,X at CPU $C1DF.\"\n\nGood. Let me also mention the flag $000F in the type notes (done).\n\nNow let me call record_mapping 4 times, then promote_mappings.\n\nI should double check the \"category\" enum values: background, interactive, decoration, enemy, player, item, other. Use \"enemy\".\n\ngroup: \"enemy_object\".\n\nLet me make the calls. They're independent; batch them.\n\nAlso, `length` for arrays: I'll use stride+count.\n\nLet me write them."}
