{"type":"thinking","text":"Now write the final report concisely.\n\nKey: mention the pitfall found (game free-runs between calls; keep it paused, use step_frame) and the arrays.\n\nReport:\n\nSheet 3 — enemy slot arrays, SMB1 World 1-1.\n\n| what | address (slot 0) | array | encoding |\n| type/ID | $0016 | $0016-$001B (stride 1, 6 slots) | enemy ID, Goomba = $06, $0B = red Koopa Troopa |\n| x low | $0087 | $0087-$008C (stride 1, 6) | low byte of level x; absolute = $006E*256 + $0087 |\n| x page | $006E | $006E-$0073 (stride 1, 6) | high byte |\n| y | $00CF | $00CF-$00D4 (stride 1, 6) | screen y |\n\nNote the player is one byte before each (x $0086, y $00CE, page $006D), because the object engine indexes these arrays with X=0 for the player; the spawner writes enemies at X=0 with the enemy-only bases.\n\nEvidence bullets.\n\nAlso mention supporting: $000F flag, $001E state, $03AE derived screen x.\n\nWrite concisely."}
{"type":"text","text":"Done — four arrays found, proven, recorded, and promoted (23 addresses now in the ROM mapping).\n\n## Sheet 3 result: SMB1 World 1-1 enemy-slot arrays\n\nThe object engine keeps the player and the enemies in the **same** zero-page arrays, indexed by slot, stride 1: **index 0 = player, indices 1–6 = enemies** (the spawner uses the enemy-only base, i.e. `STA $87,X` with X=0 = the first enemy, which is `$0086+1`). The routine at CPU `$F171` is the giveaway: `LDA $CE,X / STA $03B8,Y` (y) and `LDA $86,X / SEC / SBC $071C / STA $03AD,Y` (x).\n\n| what | address (first enemy slot) | array | encoding |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **type / ID** | **`$0016`** | `$0016`–`$001B`, stride 1, count 6 | enemy ID; World 1-1 Goomba = `$06`, `$0B` = red Koopa Troopa |\n| **horizontal** (low byte) | **`$0087`** | `$0087`–`$008C`, stride 1, count 6 | low byte of level x; absolute level x = `$006E`*256 + `$0087` |\n| **horizontal** (page) | **`$006E`** | `$006E`–`$0073`, stride 1, count 6 | high byte of level x |\n| **vertical** | **`$00CF`** | `$00CF`–`$00D4`, stride 1, count 6 | screen y of the enemy sprite (OAM y = value + 1) |\n\nSupporting bytes in the same slot struct: `$000F` = active flag (the live Goomba read 1), `$001E` = state, `$03AE` = derived on-screen x.\n\n**Evidence**\n- **x — write proven.** Goomba slot read `$0087`=34, page 1 (level x 290, screen x 174). `write_memory $0087=100` + `step_frame 4` moved the drawn Goomba's OAM x from **175 → 240/248** (screenshot: it jumped to the right edge while Mario stayed at 112); a second write of 80 put it at 219 = 256+79−116. (Note: the draw lags a frame or two — a 1-frame step made it look as if the write did nothing.)\n- **y — write proven.** `$00CF`=184 on the ground; `write_memory $00CF=140` + `step_frame 13` lifted the Goomba to OAM y **142/150/158**, with its own gravity step 140→141.\n- **type — write proven.** `$0016`=6 for the Goomba; `write_memory $0016=11` + `step_frame 3` turned it into a **red Koopa Troopa** (`list_sprites`: palette 5, CHR tiles 165–169 instead of palette 7 / 112–115; screenshot shows the red shell).\n- **page — watch proven.** A 110-frame no-input run sampling every 2 frames read `$0087` = 33,32,…,1,0 then 255,254,…,238 while `$006E` held 1 through frame 66 and flipped to 0 at the frame-68 sample — exactly the frame the low byte wrapped 0→255.\n- The spawner at `$C12F`–`$C13D` writes `STA $16,X` (type from `$06CD`), `STA $0F,X`=1 (flag), `STA $1E,X`=0 (state); `$C1AB` `STA $6E,X`; `$C1B4` `STA $87,X`; `$C1DF` `STA $CF,X` — one per-slot X across all these bases.\n\n**Method note:** with no reference I first used differential search (a 24-frame idle diff over the 2 KB left only `$0087`, `$03AE` and the OAM entries as movers), then `trace_writes` on the derived screen-x pointed straight at `$F171`, and the spawner disassembly named the field bases, each then proven by write. One practical trap worth remembering: the game free-runs between tool calls, so snapshots/diffs must be taken with the emulator paused and frames advanced only with `step_frame`/`play_input` — my first two windows were ruined by deaths that happened while I was reading.\n\n`promote_mappings` wrote all four to `mappings/sha1-33d23c2f2cfa4c9efec87f7bc1321ce3ce6c89bd.json` (0 hypotheses skipped). The emulator is back in World 1-1 and running."}
